TEST 2: CONTROLLED EXECUTION (THE TRI-STYLE CHALLENGE)
Task Instructions
Hold the following physical event strictly constant across three materially
distinct prose executions:
The Constant Event: A scout must climb through the jagged breach of a
collapsed brick factory wall, cross a fifteen-foot basement drop via a
single surviving steel I-beam, and drop into the unlit machinery room on the
other side as a passing patrol sweeps a searchlight across the building's
exterior.
Expected Deliverables
Write the event across three distinct, fully realized prose profiles (two
paragraphs each):
Profile A (Severe Kinetic Compression): High velocity, paratactic clausal
momentum, Anglo-Saxon verbs, zero internal hand-wringing, hard physical
impact.
Profile B (W-Raytraced Visual Composition): Deep chiaroscuro, value
contrast, volumetric beam scattering, graphic silhouetting,
affordance-guided movement.
Profile C (Sensory Dissonance & Physical Friction): High tactile resolution,
material deformation telegraphed through sound and vibration, defamiliarized
