Marking & Pass Criteria
Pass: All three profiles are immediately distinguishable by ear and
syntactic rhythm; all three preserve identical physical coordinates and
causal logic; all three achieve high immersion without jargon or melodrama.
Critical Failure Conditions:
Profile A becomes a bulleted list of short sentences without connective
rhythm.
Profile B pauses narrative time to describe light fixtures (the
benchmark trap).
Profile C slips into clinical terminology ("proprioceptive feedback").
